    <solution><m>W</m> for a fixed value of <m>x</m> is a
semi-circle the boundary of which is <m>y^2 + z^2 = 1</m>, for
<m>z\le 0</m>, so we may take the inner integral
to be
<me>\int_{-\sqrt{1-y^{2}}}^{0} g(x,y,z)\,dz.</me>
Lining up these stacks parallel to <m>y</m>-axis gives a slice from
<m>y=-1</m> to
<m>y=1</m> giving
<me>\int_{-1}^{1}
    \int_{-\sqrt{1-y^{2}}}^{0} g(x,y,z)\,
	dz\,dy.</me>
Finally, there is a slice for each <m>x</m> between 0 and 1, so the integral
we want is
<me>\int_{0}^{1}
  \int_{-1}^{1}
    \int_{-\sqrt{1-y^{2}}}^{0} g(x,y,z)\,
	dz\,dy\,dx.</me>



We could also write this as
<me>\int_{0}^{1}
  \int_{-1}^{0}
    \int_{-\sqrt{1-z^{2}}}^{\sqrt{1-z^{2}}} g(x,y,z)\,
	dy\,dz\,dx.</me>



</solution>
